// ================= Goethals Bridge (2017 eastbound, 2018 westbound) =================
// stations s along the eastbound carriageway (A, the southern structure) from the Elizabeth (NJ) end; the westbound structure
// (B) runs 31 m north and carries the shared-use path (C) on its north edge. Per structure (AISC/NSBA 2016, Port Authority):
// 900 ft main span between the towers (OSM pier footprints: s 954.8; the Staten Island towers 274.3 m east), 367.5 ft back
// spans to the anchor piers (Pier 2, 126 ft, with a counterweight), flanking spans 190 / 157.5 ft to Pier 3; concrete towers
// 268.5 ft high (121.8 ft above the deck), each a pair of V-shaped leg frames (one per stay plane) whose legs lean out 5°;
// 72 stays per structure in pairs (9 main + 9 back per leg frame, a triple backstay to the anchor pier), side-mounted on the
